connector spec jira, version 1
summary: Reads of a Jira Cloud site without changing it.
endpoint: base path none, hosts: any host of the catalog
auth: basic, key variable JIRA_API_TOKEN, account variable JIRA_EMAIL
limits: timeout 30s (cap), reply 10485760 bytes (cap), at most 20 pages (cap)
operations: 7
1. jira.auth.whoami: read, GET /rest/api/3/myself, writes no, cli on, mcp on
   show the account that the credentials sign in as
2. jira.projects.page: read, GET /rest/api/3/project/search, writes no, cli on, mcp on
   list one page of the projects of the source
3. jira.issues.query: read, POST /rest/api/3/search/jql, writes no, cli on, mcp on
   search the issues that match a JQL query, one page of at most 100 issues
4. jira.issues.read: read, GET /rest/api/3/issue/{issueKey}, writes no, cli on, mcp on
   print the Markdown of one Jira issue
5. jira.comments.page: read, GET /rest/api/3/issue/{issueKey}/comment, writes no, cli on, mcp on
   list one page of the comments of one Jira issue, as Markdown
6. jira.projects.all: read, GET /rest/api/3/project/search, writes no, cli off, mcp off
   read every page of the projects of the source, oldest first
7. jira.issues.tree: read, POST /rest/api/3/search/jql, writes no, cli off, mcp off
   read one search of issues for the tree of a project, oldest first
POST reads: 2
1. jira.issues.query: POST /rest/api/3/search/jql, body from slots: jql, limit
2. jira.issues.tree: POST /rest/api/3/search/jql, body from slots: jql, limit, nextPageToken
Body paging: 2
1. jira.issues.query: cursor in body (limit), at most 1 pages
2. jira.issues.tree: cursor in body (nextPageToken), at most 5 pages
Required fields: 2
1. jira.auth.whoami: required active, displayName
2. jira.issues.read: formats labels=strings
Issue keys: 2
1. jira.issues.read: path parameter issueKey
2. jira.comments.page: path parameter issueKey
Page ends: 5
1. jira.projects.page: last of /isLast; cut to limit
2. jira.issues.query: last of /isLast; cut to limit; truncated of /nextPageToken and /isLast
3. jira.comments.page: cut to limit
4. jira.projects.all: last of /isLast; cut to maxResults
5. jira.issues.tree: last of /isLast; cut to limit; truncated of /nextPageToken and /isLast
Key echoes: 1
1. jira.issues.read: issueKey equals /key
Built IDs: 3
1. jira.issues.query: projectKey as project key of /key
2. jira.issues.read: collectionId as collection ID of /key; id as issue ID of /key; projectKey as project key of /key; url as browse URL of /key
3. jira.issues.tree: url as browse URL of /key
Document layouts: 1
1. jira.issues.read: title title, 13 lines, body description as Description
Query keys: 2
1. jira.projects.page: limit as maxResults, offset as startAt
2. jira.comments.page: limit as maxResults, offset as startAt
Bundled mapping: 7
1. jira.auth.whoami: catalog jira.whoami
2. jira.projects.page: catalog jira.projects.list
3. jira.issues.query: catalog jira.issues.search
4. jira.issues.read: catalog jira.issues.get
5. jira.comments.page: catalog jira.comments.list
6. jira.projects.all: no catalog row, cli off, mcp off
7. jira.issues.tree: no catalog row, cli off, mcp off
